does_not_resolve_to_a_builtin | context awareness: goto on `holder.abs` answers `None` while a plain `abs` call still answers the builtin | | edge_navigation_handles_cr_and_crlf_line_endings | line endings: lone CR and CRLF line starts, comment termination, goto, references and completion after the comment | | edge_completions_at_the_opening_quote_and_comment_marker_are_empty | boundary: a caret on the opening quote or on the first `/` of `//` is inside text/comment | | edge_malformed_source_error_carries_the_lexer_span | malformed source: the error keeps both `Unterminated string` and its `1:5` span | | edge_goto_definition_on_object_method_call_resolves_to_the_method_declaration | object navigation: `Greeter.greet()` resolves to `to can greet`, and its references include the call | | edge_goto_definition_on_a_this_method_call_resolves_to_the_method_declaration | object navigation: `this.greet()` resolves to the method declaration | | edge_object_method_and_field_of_the_same_name_stay_distinct | duplicate names: `Row.name` is the field while `Row.name()` is the method, and their references stay separate | | edge_object_field_declared_after_its_method_still_wins_a_bare_read | duplicate names: a bare `name` read resolves to `has name` even when `to can name()` is declared first, while the call still resolves to the method | | edge_bare_method_call_prefers_the_method_over_a_same_named_field | duplicate names: a bare `b()` call resolves to the method while the field's references stay separate | | edge_navigation_rejects_a_position_past_the_file | out of bounds: line `99` in a one-line file is a clean `Err` from all three, never a panic |  ### Mandatory edge-case matrix  | Row | Covered? | |---|---| | empty | covered by `edge_empty_source_answers_without_failing` | | singleton | covered by the one-use fixtures; a single reference is asserted exactly | | boundary | covered by EOF-without-newline; cursor at column `len + 1`; end-of-comment and unterminated-comment positio